Debug.Assert(RET == index || RET == -1);
</code>
This assertion statement is related to the Remove method of the ArrayList class in C#. It checks whether the return value (index of the object that was removed or -1 if the object was not found) is equal to the old value of the index (i.e., the first index where the object was found before it was removed), which is the desired behavior of the Remove method.
--------------------
Debug.Assert(OLD(IndexOf(obj)) != -1 || IndexOf(obj) == -1);
</code>
--------------------
Debug.Assert(RET == index || Old(index) == -1);
</code>

This statement is derived from the comment "@@@ first index of obj never decreases except the case when it becomes -1" present in the following snippet:

```cs
public virtual void Remove(Object obj)
{
    int index = IndexOf(obj);
    if (index >= 0)
        RemoveAt(index);

    // @@@ first index of obj never decreases except the case when it becomes -1
}
```
